 "drivingQuestion": "From where is it derived that the Sabbatical year begins in Tishrei?",
 "outcome": "resolved",
 "outcomeNote": "The source is given; the next unit tests the gezera shava.",
 "continuesQuestionOf": null,
 "segments": [
  {
   "id": "rosh_hashanah.8b.6",
   "daf": "8b",
   "sentenceId": 5,
   "he": "וְלַשְּׁמִיטִּין. מְנָלַן? דִּכְתִיב: ״וּבַשָּׁנָה הַשְּׁבִיעִית שַׁבַּת שַׁבָּתוֹן יִהְיֶה לָאָרֶץ״, וְגָמַר ״שָׁנָה״ ״שָׁנָה״ מִתִּשְׁרִי, דִּכְתִיב: ״מֵרֵאשִׁית הַשָּׁנָה״.",
   "en": "§ The mishna teaches: The first of Tishrei is also the New Year «for» calculating «Sabbatical Years.» The Gemara asks: «From where do we» derive this? «As it is written: “But in the seventh year shall be a Shabbat of solemn rest for the land”» (Leviticus 25:4), «and» we «learn» by way of a verbal analogy between one instance of the word «“year”» and another instance of the word «“year”» that the year begins for this purpose «from Tishrei, as it is written: “From the beginning of the year”» (Deuteronomy 11:12). The latter verse is referring to the year that begins at the onset of the rainy season, i.e., Tishrei."
  }
 ],
